  "summary": "I added a \"Tour\" button below the canvas, at left:8px, top:368px. Clicking it focuses each planet from Mercury outwards for about 3 seconds each, with the info panel showing. After Uranus it returns to the overview. While touring the button reads \"Stop tour\", and clicking it returns to the overview. I also added `touring: boolean` to `window.__TASK_STATE__`. Typecheck passes and the render shows the Tour button below the canvas with no errors. I did not run the tour itself, so the timing, the button text change and the return to overview are untested. The 3 seconds per planet includes the 1.5 second camera move and runs on real time, so Pause doesn't affect it. Clicking a planet, clicking empty space, pressing Escape, or calling `__focusPlanet` or `__unfocus` also ends the tour."
